      "title": "Add an \"Updated At\" timestamp column so readers can spot new roles",
      "description": "The `Date Posted` column is day-level only, so when new roles get added between refreshes there's no way to tell which rows are new since my last visit — I have to re-scan the whole table from the top and remember where I left off.\n\nProposal: add a column (e.g. `Updated At`) showing the date + time each row was added or updated by the bot, like:\n\n| Company | Job Title | Location | Date Posted | Updated At |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Company A | ... | ... | Sep 29 | Sep 29, 13:53 |\n| Company B | ... | ... | Sep 29 | Sep 29, 17:54 |\n\nThis should be feasible since the bot already knows when it inserts each row (the timestamp is implicit in the commit history today) — persisting it per-row just makes it visible to everyone. Readers could then instantly see what's new since their last refresh.",
